# root SSH authorized_keys — ADD YOUR OWN PUBLIC KEY HERE before building.
#
# This file ships in the rootfs and controls who can SSH in as root. sshd is
# configured key-only (PasswordAuthentication no, see ../../etc/ssh/sshd_config),
# so until you add a key here, root SSH login is disabled and you must use the
# serial console (mini-USB, 115200 8N1).
#
# Paste your ed25519/RSA public key on its own line below, e.g.:
#   ssh-ed25519 AAAA... you@host
#
# Generate one with:  ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f ~/.ssh/odo-miner
# then append ~/.ssh/odo-miner.pub here.
